{
  "slug": "a-simple-proof-of-the-cap-theorem",
  "title": "A Simple Proof of the CAP Theorem",
  "subtitle": "CAP in one scenario (no fluff)",
  "date": "2026-01-03",
  "canonical": "https://pradyumnachippigiri.substack.com/p/a-simple-proof-of-the-cap-theorem",
  "body_html": "<p>Appreciate you reading this newsletter, I am writing as I learn too. I hope the content and resources are helping you level up as an engineer. If you want me to write about something specific, just message me or comment on the post.</p><blockquote><p><strong>Note:</strong> This article on was originally published on my blog -<strong> </strong><a href=\"https://pradyumnachippigiri.dev/blogs/cap-theorm\">https://pradyumnachippigiri.dev/blogs/cap-theorm</a></p></blockquote><h2>Here’s what I learned this week</h2><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://pradyumnachippigiri.dev/til/system-design/2-random-cache-eviction\">2-random cache eviction</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://pradyumnachippigiri.dev/til/frontend/image-optimize\">Ways to load images faster on web pages</a></p></li></ul><div><hr></div><p>Let’s start by understanding the basic definition of CAP, and then lets delve deep to understand the what, why and how.</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!GfR7!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa08391ee-87b5-4982-95df-282696b1d532_1920x872.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!GfR7!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa08391ee-87b5-4982-95df-282696b1d532_1920x872.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!GfR7!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa08391ee-87b5-4982-95df-282696b1d532_1920x872.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!GfR7!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa08391ee-87b5-4982-95df-282696b1d532_1920x872.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!GfR7!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa08391ee-87b5-4982-95df-282696b1d532_1920x872.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!GfR7!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa08391ee-87b5-4982-95df-282696b1d532_1920x872.png\" width=\"1456\" height=\"661\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/a08391ee-87b5-4982-95df-282696b1d532_1920x872.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:661,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:null,&quot;alt&quot;:&quot;CAP Theorm Illustration&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:null,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:true,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"CAP Theorm Illustration\" title=\"CAP Theorm Illustration\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!GfR7!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa08391ee-87b5-4982-95df-282696b1d532_1920x872.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!GfR7!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa08391ee-87b5-4982-95df-282696b1d532_1920x872.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!GfR7!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa08391ee-87b5-4982-95df-282696b1d532_1920x872.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!GfR7!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa08391ee-87b5-4982-95df-282696b1d532_1920x872.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" fetchpriority=\"high\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>CAP Theorem states that in a distributed system, you can have only 2 out of the 3 of the following properties:</p><h2>Consistency</h2><p>Every read receives the most recent write or an error. Consistency means that all clients see the same data at the same time, no matter which node they connect to. For this to happen, whenever data is written to one node, it must be instantly forwarded or replicated to all the other nodes in the system before the write is deemed succesfull. Consistency as defined in the CAP theorem is quite different from the consistency guaranteed in ACID database transactions.[</p><h2>Availability</h2><p>Every request received by a non-failing node in the system must result in a response, without the guarantee that it contains the most recent version of the data.</p><h2>Partition Tolerance</h2><p>The system continues to operate despite arbitrary message loss or failure of part of the system (i.e., network partitions between nodes).</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rdQv!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F9ff56eb6-2d24-42aa-8325-95513c55326c_1482x1368.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rdQv!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F9ff56eb6-2d24-42aa-8325-95513c55326c_1482x1368.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rdQv!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F9ff56eb6-2d24-42aa-8325-95513c55326c_1482x1368.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rdQv!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F9ff56eb6-2d24-42aa-8325-95513c55326c_1482x1368.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rdQv!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F9ff56eb6-2d24-42aa-8325-95513c55326c_1482x1368.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rdQv!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F9ff56eb6-2d24-42aa-8325-95513c55326c_1482x1368.png\" width=\"1456\" height=\"1344\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/9ff56eb6-2d24-42aa-8325-95513c55326c_1482x1368.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:1344,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:null,&quot;alt&quot;:&quot;CAP Theorm Illustration&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:null,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"CAP Theorm Illustration\" title=\"CAP Theorm Illustration\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rdQv!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F9ff56eb6-2d24-42aa-8325-95513c55326c_1482x1368.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rdQv!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F9ff56eb6-2d24-42aa-8325-95513c55326c_1482x1368.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rdQv!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F9ff56eb6-2d24-42aa-8325-95513c55326c_1482x1368.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rdQv!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F9ff56eb6-2d24-42aa-8325-95513c55326c_1482x1368.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>In the real world, network failures are inevitable. Cables are cut, routers fail, and packets are dropped. Therefore, Partition Tolerance (P) is a requirement, not a choice.</p><p>When a partition occurs, we are left with a binary choice: Consistency (CP) or Availability (AP).</p><p>To be honest, i just picked the above definitions from <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CAP_theorem\">Wikipedia</a> and pasted them here, as they have stated it beautifully.</p><p>So now from the above definitions, the first question that may arise to you is :</p><blockquote><p>Why cant there be a system with both consistency and availability ?</p></blockquote><p>I thought that the CAP theorem was like this complicated topic in distributed systems theory.</p><p>It turns out that (even though it is a somewhat useful thing!) it is a really simple result to prove. Basically:</p><p>To understand why we can’t have all three, let’s look at a practical example</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!hImG!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fce11b8ac-defe-4032-a39a-b9cf43ac7e39_1620x486.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!hImG!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fce11b8ac-defe-4032-a39a-b9cf43ac7e39_1620x486.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!hImG!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fce11b8ac-defe-4032-a39a-b9cf43ac7e39_1620x486.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!hImG!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fce11b8ac-defe-4032-a39a-b9cf43ac7e39_1620x486.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!hImG!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fce11b8ac-defe-4032-a39a-b9cf43ac7e39_1620x486.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!hImG!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fce11b8ac-defe-4032-a39a-b9cf43ac7e39_1620x486.png\" width=\"1456\" height=\"437\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/ce11b8ac-defe-4032-a39a-b9cf43ac7e39_1620x486.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:437,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:null,&quot;alt&quot;:&quot;Cluster Partition&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:null,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"Cluster Partition\" title=\"Cluster Partition\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!hImG!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fce11b8ac-defe-4032-a39a-b9cf43ac7e39_1620x486.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!hImG!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fce11b8ac-defe-4032-a39a-b9cf43ac7e39_1620x486.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!hImG!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fce11b8ac-defe-4032-a39a-b9cf43ac7e39_1620x486.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!hImG!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fce11b8ac-defe-4032-a39a-b9cf43ac7e39_1620x486.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>Imagine a distributed system with two clusters located in different regions: Asia(the cluster on the left) and the USA(the cluster on the right). Under normal conditions, they sync perfectly. But then, a submarine cable is damaged, and the two regions lose connection. They are now “partitioned.”</p><p>A user in Asia updates their profile. Since the Asia cluster cannot talk to the USA cluster, we have to make a design choice:</p><ul><li><p><strong>The CP Choice (Consistency):</strong><br>We want the USA user to see the updated data. But because the network is broken, we can’t sync the update. To maintain consistency, we must return an error to the USA user (decreasing Availability). We’d rather show a “Service Unavailable” message than show the wrong data.</p></li></ul><ul><li><p><strong>The AP Choice (Availability)</strong>:<br>We want the system to have zero downtime. Even though the clusters can’t talk, the USA cluster still responds to the user. However, the user sees the old, stale data because the Asia update hasn’t arrived yet. The system is available, but the data is inconsistent.</p></li></ul><h2>Which one should you choose ?</h2><p>The choice totaly depends on the usecase of the application.</p><p><strong>CP based Applications</strong></p><ul><li><p>Ticket booking system (say a person booked a ticket, and partition happens, and if the pther person is able to see old data then even he can book the ticket, which is catastrophic, hence it has to be strongly consistent)</p></li><li><p>Financial banking Banking Applications.</p></li></ul><p>These applications need strong consitency.</p><p><strong>AP based Applications</strong></p><ul><li><p>Social Media App (if a person updates his name on his profile, and if you dont see it immediately (the correct data) thats okay, no one cares even if you sees stale data for sometime (but if the application goes down then thats not acceptable.))</p></li><li><p>Business review service etc.</p><div class=\"subscription-widget-wrap-editor\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://pradyumnachippigiri.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe&quot;,&quot;language&quot;:&quot;en&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"SubscribeWidgetToDOM\"><div class=\"subscription-widget show-subscribe\"><div class=\"preamble\"><p class=\"cta-caption\">Thanks for reading LevelYouUp! Subscribe for free to receive new posts and support my work.</p></div><form class=\"subscription-widget-subscribe\"><input type=\"email\" class=\"email-input\" name=\"email\" placeholder=\"Type your email…\" tabindex=\"-1\"><input type=\"submit\" class=\"button primary\" value=\"Subscribe\"><div class=\"fake-input-wrapper\"><div class=\"fake-input\"></div><div class=\"fake-button\"></div></div></form></div></div></li></ul><h2>Tools or types od DB for each usecase ?</h2><p><strong>CP based Applications</strong></p><p>These kind of applications that demand strong consistency the db which satisfy these are :</p><ul><li><p>Postgres</p></li><li><p>RDBMS</p></li></ul><p><strong>AP based Applications</strong></p><p>these kind of applications which demand availability and where eventual consistency is okay then we use :</p><ul><li><p>DynamoDB</p></li><li><p>Cassandra</p></li></ul><h2>Extended version of CAP</h2><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!2V_U!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F17bfd76d-82f0-465e-b9ff-c7a63ccc2b7d_1620x1228.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!2V_U!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F17bfd76d-82f0-465e-b9ff-c7a63ccc2b7d_1620x1228.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!2V_U!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F17bfd76d-82f0-465e-b9ff-c7a63ccc2b7d_1620x1228.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!2V_U!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F17bfd76d-82f0-465e-b9ff-c7a63ccc2b7d_1620x1228.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!2V_U!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F17bfd76d-82f0-465e-b9ff-c7a63ccc2b7d_1620x1228.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!2V_U!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F17bfd76d-82f0-465e-b9ff-c7a63ccc2b7d_1620x1228.png\" width=\"1456\" height=\"1104\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/17bfd76d-82f0-465e-b9ff-c7a63ccc2b7d_1620x1228.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:1104,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:null,&quot;alt&quot;:&quot;PACELC Therorem&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:null,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"PACELC Therorem\" title=\"PACELC Therorem\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!2V_U!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F17bfd76d-82f0-465e-b9ff-c7a63ccc2b7d_1620x1228.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!2V_U!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F17bfd76d-82f0-465e-b9ff-c7a63ccc2b7d_1620x1228.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!2V_U!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F17bfd76d-82f0-465e-b9ff-c7a63ccc2b7d_1620x1228.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!2V_U!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F17bfd76d-82f0-465e-b9ff-c7a63ccc2b7d_1620x1228.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>PACELC is another theorem, an extension of the CAP theorem. Wikipedia states that in the case of network partitioning (P) in a distributed computer system, one has to choose between availability (A) and consistency (C) (as per the CAP theorem), but else (E), even when the system is running normally in the absence of partitions, one has to choose between latency (L) and loss of consistency (C).</p><p>Hope you got a fair understanding of the CAP theorem, if you liked it please do subscribe and consider sharing it with your friends on social media if you found this helpful.</p><div class=\"subscription-widget-wrap-editor\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://pradyumnachippigiri.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe&quot;,&quot;language&quot;:&quot;en&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"SubscribeWidgetToDOM\"><div class=\"subscription-widget show-subscribe\"><div class=\"preamble\"><p class=\"cta-caption\">Thanks for reading LevelYouUp! Subscribe for free to receive new posts and support my work.</p></div><form class=\"subscription-widget-subscribe\"><input type=\"email\" class=\"email-input\" name=\"email\" placeholder=\"Type your email…\" tabindex=\"-1\"><input type=\"submit\" class=\"button primary\" value=\"Subscribe\"><div class=\"fake-input-wrapper\"><div class=\"fake-input\"></div><div class=\"fake-button\"></div></div></form></div></div>"
}